  "content": {
    "id": "p50-q26-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "26",
    "prompt": "Two ancient armies are about to battle each other.\nThe Egyptians are in town.\nThe Romans are 1 km away from the town.\nThe armies begin walking towards each other.\nThe Egyptians walk at a pace of 3 km/h and the Romans walk at a pace of 4 km/h.\nFor how long will they walk before the battle begins?\n(Hint: let the equations represent distance from the town; $d=st$.)\nGive an exact time in hours, or a time in minutes and seconds rounded to the nearest second.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{7}$ hour, approximately 8 minutes 34 seconds.",
      "worked": "Let $t$ be the time in hours after both armies start walking and $d$ their distance from town in kilometres.\n\nThe Egyptians move away from town; the Romans approach it:\n$$\\begin{align*}d&=3t &&(1)\\\\d&=1-4t &&(2)\\end{align*}$$\nAt their meeting point:\n$$\\begin{align*}3t&=1-4t\\\\7t&=1\\\\t&=\\frac{1}{7}\\end{align*}$$\nThey walk for $\\frac{1}{7}$ hour. This is $\\frac{3600}{7}$ seconds, approximately 8 minutes 34 seconds.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
